"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(n * log(n)) complexity by time and O(n * log(n)) by space.

I liked this problem. 
It just requires sitting down and thinking it through. 
Initially, I tried a greedy approach to adjust the distances, but that doesn't work in every case. 
Fortunately, there are only two possible actions, so we can easily examine all the options.
It is always advantageous to transform one number into any other; this results in a distance of 0. 
Essentially, we have two operations that allow us to remove two numbers from the overall list.
In this scenario, we can greedily select the ones that contribute the most to the total score.
"""

class Solution:
    def minimizeSum(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        nums.sort()
        return min(nums[-1] - nums[2], nums[-2] - nums[1], nums[-3] - nums[0])
